  "output": {
    "svg": "architecture.svg",
    "medium": "documentation and notebook",
    "alt_text": "A model proposes only a policy resource identifier. Trusted runtime identity and an application tool contract enter current resource policy. A credential broker consults vault metadata but never secret bytes, then issues an opaque one-use lease. The credential executor reauthorizes, atomically claims the lease, materializes the exact secret version into an ephemeral handle, and calls one external provider. Only a bounded result or generic error returns. Secret lifecycle, lease state, redacted receipts, and explicit outcomes support every decision."
  },
